---
/* About — client-first StoryBrand page (Phase 3 Plan 02, PAGES-03/PAGES-08/OPS-06).
   Spine (D-05): the client's world + the fear of the wrong counsel → BSV as the
   guide with a plan (team approach, partner access, transaction focus) → firm
   substance as proof ("why a boutique" — M&A/IP/Tax focus, senior pedigrees,
   Chambers) → "Based in San Francisco" → a closing CTA
   toward /contact with onward links to /attorneys and /practice-areas.

   Constraints honored:
   - D-06: verifiable facts only — NO invented founding year or origin narrative.
     Every substance claim below traces to FIRM_BRIEF.md.
   - D-36: the "where we work" beat shows only SITE.basedIn ("Based in San
     Francisco.") with no street address, and stays SILENT on the office/virtual
     arrangement — no "virtual firm" wording, no mention of having no offices.
   - Token-only Tailwind v4 namespace utilities (text-text / bg-bg / text-accent) —
     no arbitrary-value color form, no hardcoded hex.
   - OPS-06: the prose lives in plain, clearly separated paragraphs so a non-coding
     author (Jon) can edit the copy directly via the GitHub web editor. */
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Eyebrow from '../components/ui/Eyebrow.astro';
import TextLink from '../components/ui/TextLink.astro';
import CtaBlock from '../components/sections/CtaBlock.astro';
import { SITE } from '../lib/site';

/* The "guide with a plan" beat — the three FIRM_BRIEF client fears, mapped to how
   BSV answers each. Competence → partner-led teams; experience → deep transaction
   record; responsiveness → moves at the deal's pace. */
const plan = [
  {
    title: 'Partner-led teams',
    body: 'Senior attorneys do the work. You get partner-level judgment on every issue — not a matter handed down to a rotating cast of junior associates.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Deep transaction experience',
    body: 'We focus on M&A, IP and technology transactions, and tax — and we have closed the kind of deal you are running, on both the buy and sell side.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Moves at your deal’s pace',
    body: 'Transactions have momentum. We staff lean and respond fast, so legal is never the reason a deal slows down.',
  },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About BSV Law"
  description="Belcher, Smolen & Van Loo LLP — a boutique California law firm focused on M&A, IP & technology transactions, and tax for the companies building what's next."
>
  <!-- 1. The client's world + the fear of the wrong counsel (StoryBrand opening) -->
  <section class="bg-bg py-section">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-gutter">
      <Eyebrow>About the firm</Eyebrow>
      <h1 class="mt-3 text-h1 font-bold text-text">
        A complex transaction deserves a team that treats it like their only one.
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-6 text-body-lg text-text-muted">
        When you are running an acquisition, a financing, a licensing deal, or a
        cross-border tax matter, the hardest decision often comes first: who do you
        trust to handle it? The wrong counsel is slow, learns on your dime, or hands
        your matter to whoever is free that week.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-body-lg text-text-muted">
        Belcher, Smolen &amp; Van Loo is a boutique built to be the opposite of that.
        We are a small group of senior, transaction-focused attorneys, and we give
        every matter the priority of a firm where the partners do the work themselves.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 2. BSV as the guide with a plan -->
  <section class="bg-bg py-section">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-gutter">
      <Eyebrow>How we work</Eyebrow>
      <h2 class="mt-3 max-w-3xl text-h2 font-bold text-text">
        Team work to get good results.
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-4 max-w-3xl text-body-lg text-text-muted">
        Our advantage is structural. A boutique gives every client the attention and
        priority a large firm reserves for its biggest accounts — and unlike a
        generalist boutique, we concentrate on the transactions we know best.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-10 grid gap-8 sm:grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-3">
        {
          plan.map((point) => (
            <div>
              <span class="block h-1 w-10 rounded-full bg-accent" aria-hidden="true" />
              <h3 class="mt-4 text-h3 font-bold text-text" set:html={point.title} />
              <p class="mt-3 text-body text-text-muted">{point.body}</p>
            </div>
          ))
        }
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 3. Firm substance as proof — "why a boutique" (verifiable facts only, D-06) -->
  <section class="bg-bg py-section">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-gutter">
      <Eyebrow>Why a boutique</Eyebrow>
      <h2 class="mt-3 text-h2 font-bold text-text">
        Specialists, not generalists.
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-6 text-body-lg text-text-muted">
        Our practice is disciplined around three areas: mergers and acquisitions,
        intellectual property and technology transactions, and tax. We serve technology,
        life sciences, cryptocurrency, FinTech, and AI companies — and their investors,
        acquirers, and counterparties.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-body-lg text-text-muted">
        That focus is backed by senior pedigrees. Our partners advise on complex M&amp;A
        for public and private acquirers, private equity firms, and venture-backed
        companies; on patent strategy, licensing, open-source, and data-security matters;
        and on M&amp;A, international, and cryptocurrency tax — including tax-free
        reorganizations and token sales. Among us we have practiced at Linklaters,
        Dechert, and Dewey &amp; LeBoeuf, clerked on the Federal Circuit, and built a
        crypto-tax practice since 2017.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-body-lg text-text-muted">
        When a matter calls for expertise outside our lane — antitrust, for example — we
        assemble a team of elite specialists rather than over-claim. And we are clear
        about cost: we bill hourly, paired with an estimate of the total cost for each
        engagement, so you are never left guessing.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-body-lg text-text-muted">
        Our work has been recognized in the Chambers USA Spotlight 2026 as a leading firm
        ranked in Mergers &amp; Acquisitions — but the proof clients value most is the
        deals we have closed and the partners who answer the phone.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 4. Where we work — San Francisco base (D-36: silent on the office arrangement) -->
  <section class="bg-bg py-section">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-gutter">
      <Eyebrow>Where we work</Eyebrow>
      <h2 class="mt-3 text-h2 font-bold text-text">{SITE.basedIn}</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-body-lg text-text-muted">
        We work with clients building across the technology, life sciences, FinTech,
        and cryptocurrency industries, and we are reachable by phone and email
        throughout your deal.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 5. Closing CTA + onward links (StoryBrand loop close, D-07) -->
  <CtaBlock
    heading="Let’s talk about your transaction."
    body="Tell us what you are working on, and we will tell you straight whether we are the right team for it."
    ctaLabel="Start a conversation"
    ctaHref="/contact"
  />

  <section class="bg-bg pb-section">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-gutter text-center">
      <p class="text-body text-text-muted">
        Or meet <TextLink href="/attorneys">the team</TextLink> and explore our
        <TextLink href="/practice-areas">practice areas</TextLink>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
